### Drill 6: Projected Volumes via ConfigMaps & Secrets (`04-configmap-secret/`)

Mounting ConfigMaps and Secrets as volume files provides declarative, file-based configuration injection with
granular UNIX file permissions (`defaultMode`).

#### Step 1: Create the ConfigMap and Secret Imperatively

In the CKA exam, create configuration resources imperatively for maximum speed:

```bash
cd {{ cka_lab_volumes_dir }}/04-configmap-secret

# Create ConfigMap with multiple keys
kubectl create configmap app-runtime-config \
  --from-literal=app.conf="server_port=8080"$'\n'"log_level=info"$'\n'"cache_ttl=300" \
  --from-literal=feature-flags.json='{"enableMetrics": true, "betaFeatures": false}'

# Create Secret with credentials
kubectl create secret generic api-auth-credentials \
  --from-literal=api-token.txt="cka-lab-mock-api-token-value" \
  --from-literal=service-account-config.json='{"auth_type": "service_account"}'
```

#### Step 2: Mount ConfigMap as Volume Files (`defaultMode: 0644`)

Each key in the ConfigMap automatically becomes an individual file inside `mountPath`:

```yaml
cat <<'EOF' > configmap-volume-pod.yaml
apiVersion: v1
kind: Pod
metadata:
  name: configmap-volume-pod
  namespace: default
spec:
  containers:
    - name: app
      image: busybox:1.36
      command: ["sh", "-c", "cat /etc/config/app.conf && sleep 3600"]
      volumeMounts:
        - name: config-volume
          mountPath: /etc/config
          readOnly: true
  volumes:
    - name: config-volume
      configMap:
        name: app-runtime-config
        defaultMode: 0644
EOF

kubectl apply -f configmap-volume-pod.yaml
kubectl wait --for=condition=Ready pod/configmap-volume-pod --timeout=60s

# Verify mounted files and permissions (-rw-r--r--)
kubectl exec configmap-volume-pod -- ls -lah /etc/config
kubectl exec configmap-volume-pod -- cat /etc/config/app.conf
```

#### Step 3: Restrictive Secret Volume Permissions (`defaultMode: 0400` / `256`)

In CKA security drills, sensitive credentials mounted from Secrets must often have strict read-only permissions
(`0400` / decimal `256`):

```yaml
cat <<'EOF' > secret-volume-pod.yaml
apiVersion: v1
kind: Pod
metadata:
  name: secret-volume-pod
  namespace: default
spec:
  containers:
    - name: api-client
      image: busybox:1.36
      command: ["sh", "-c", "ls -l /etc/secrets && sleep 3600"]
      volumeMounts:
        - name: secret-volume
          mountPath: /etc/secrets
          readOnly: true
  volumes:
    - name: secret-volume
      secret:
        secretName: api-auth-credentials
        defaultMode: 256  # 0400 in octal is 256 in decimal
EOF

kubectl apply -f secret-volume-pod.yaml
kubectl wait --for=condition=Ready pod/secret-volume-pod --timeout=60s

# Verify strict read-only permissions (-r--------)
kubectl exec secret-volume-pod -- ls -l /etc/secrets
kubectl exec secret-volume-pod -- cat /etc/secrets/api-token.txt
```

