### Drill 8: Dynamic NFS CSI Driver & StorageClasses (`09-nfs-csi/`)

Dynamic volume provisioning eliminates the need to manually author static PersistentVolumes. When a PVC requests
a `storageClassName`, the CSI storage provisioner creates the volume and PV automatically.

#### Step 1: Deploy Dynamic StorageClass and Claim

```bash
cd {{ cka_lab_volumes_dir }}

# Deploy Dynamic NFS StorageClass & ReadWriteMany PVC
kubectl apply -f 09-nfs-csi/03-nfs-csi-sc.yaml
kubectl apply -f 09-nfs-csi/04-nfs-dynamic-pvc.yaml

# Verify StorageClass and PVC binding
kubectl get sc {{ cka_lab_nfs_csi_storage_class | default('nfs-csi') }}
kubectl get pvc nfs-dynamic-claim
```

#### Step 2: Mount in Multi-Replica Workload & Verify Shared Data

```bash
kubectl apply -f 09-nfs-csi/05-nfs-shared-deployment.yaml
kubectl rollout status deployment/nfs-shared-app --timeout=60s
kubectl get pods -l app=nfs-shared-app -o wide
```

